WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.536
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show
at Home Edition."

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:07.240
[ Laughs ] Are you focused?
-Yeah.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.277
-[ Laughs ] Are you happy?
-Yeah.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.312
-Well, you look like
you were serious.

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:14.948
Oh, I didn't See your face.
-Nope.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.616
-What?
-I know.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.618
But -- But you know what?
-What?

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:21.988
-I'm pretending to because --
just want to.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.057
-Yeah. Hi, Gary.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.859
You see -- You want the ball?
You want the ball?

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:28.360
Go! Go!

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.296
Hey, guys, we have
a great show tonight.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.966
A surprise from
Will Ferrell and Kristen Wiig

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:36.936
later in the show, but our guest
is Taraji P. Henson.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:39.505
Our first guest
is Taraji P. Henson.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.507
She -- You know her from
"Empire" and her movies.

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:45.912
Her charity is the
Boris L. Henson foundation.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:50.082
Basically, it's based
on her dad, who, um --

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:51.483
No. It's upside down.

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:53.953
-[ Laughs ]
-It's funny.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.721
You can just text --

00:00:55.721 --> 00:01:00.360
text "NOSTIGMA" to 707070
for Taraji's charity.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.961
It's a really cool charity.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.662
Thank you, Winnie,
for drawing these out.

00:01:03.662 --> 00:01:06.532
Also we have Dua Lipa,
whose album

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:09.669
"Future Nostalgia"
is out right now.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.303
And she's just crushing it.

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:14.474
And her charity is --
Can you help me?

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:15.942
Are you focused again?
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:22.215
-UNICEF.org. We love Dua Lipa.
And, um, what else do we have?

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.150
Maybe we'll check in --
That's right.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.819
Franny, you did a great job
drawing that.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:30.123
Uh, let's go to some -- some
monologue jokes right now.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.390
Here we go.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:35.995
♪♪

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.197
-Welcome to "Tonight Show:
Home Edition."

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:41.167
Well, guys, tonight marked
the start of Passover.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.836
It's a holiday that celebrates
the miracles of Moses like

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:47.473
parting the Red Sea and
finding toilet paper at Target.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:49.842
Yeah, it's a big week,
with Passover starting tonight

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.577
and Easter on Sunday.

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:53.045
If your family celebrates both,

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:58.317
be sure to pick up a pack of
the all-new gefilte-fish Peeps.

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.687
This should be great --
opera singer Andrea Bocelli

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.455
is going to perform live
on Easter

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.757
from an empty cathedral
in Italy...

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:10.496
or his living room if he changes
the background on his Zoom.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.198
Some big 2020 news.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.833
Earlier today, Bernie Sanders

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.935
dropped out of
the presidential race.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.803
I'm going to miss having Bernie
in the race 'cause if there's

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:20.806
one person who's been my spirit
animal during this pandemic,

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:23.876
it's Bernie Sanders.

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:26.212
The Pulitzer Prize board
has delayed announcing

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.314
this year's winners
by two weeks.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.082
See? Don't feel bad.

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:32.251
The Pulitzer Prize people
aren't getting any reading done

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:35.020
during quarantine, either.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.556
Yesterday, a record-low number
of people at airports

00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:39.859
were checked by the TSA.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.894
At some airports,
the agents were so bored,

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:44.563
they started
frisking themselves.

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:48.100
"Now you, Larry. You get me."

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.036
That's right.
Airports are pretty much empty,

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.604
but when you walk
into the bathroom

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:56.409
somehow every stall
is already taken.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.678
Well, Disney's floating
the idea of checking people's

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.413
temperatures at the gates
when the parks reopen.

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:05.184
Yeah. Disney said they take this
pandemic extremely seriously

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:08.555
and then handed a thermometer
to a six-foot mouse in a tuxedo.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.826
-[ Chuckles ]
-Some TV news.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.562
We got a little giggle there
from my wife.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.497
Thanks, Nancy. Some TV news.

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:21.100
CBS is starting a weekly
"Sunday Movie Night"

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.337
showing classic films like
"Forrest Gump" and "Titanic."

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.973
It's perfect if you love those
movies but always dreamed of

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:30.776
seeing them interrupted
by six car commercials.

00:03:30.776 --> 00:03:32.578
I heard you can now get takeout

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.881
from some of the nicest
restaurants in the world.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.815
So finally you can eat
roasted quail

00:03:36.815 --> 00:03:39.452
with a side of wild seaweed
out of a bag

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.788
while you watch
"Wheel of Fortune."

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.859
"Buy a vowel.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:50.063
All right. Now your turn, Larry.
You frisk me."

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.865
I saw that Panera
is launching Panera Grocery

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:55.434
where they're now selling
basic grocery-store items.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.302
And this is cool.

00:03:57.302 --> 00:03:59.304
[ Laughs ]

00:03:59.304 --> 00:04:03.176
It's not even that funny.
I don't know why I'm laughing.

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:06.279
Sometimes you just need a joke
to make you laugh.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.681
I saw that Panera
is launching Panera Grocery

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.849
where they're now selling
basic grocery-store items.

00:04:10.849 --> 00:04:13.486
[ Laughs ]

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.554
And this is cool.
At the checkout...

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:17.457
[ Laughs ]

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.663
I saw that Panera
is launching Panera Grocery

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:26.132
where they're now selling
basic grocery-store items.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.867
And this is cool.
At the checkout,

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:30.069
they put all your items
in a bread bowl.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.238
[ Laughs ]

00:04:38.143 --> 00:04:42.048
Bread bowls. Oh, my gosh.
That was -- That's hilarious.

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:48.087
Uh -- [ Laughs ]
Remember we had chowder

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.890
in a bread bowl
or something in Boston?

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.758
-Oh, yeah. At the airport.
-At the airport.

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:54.560
It was a big deal, man.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.829
It, like, reinvented...
restaurants, bread bowls.

00:04:57.829 --> 00:05:00.198
You can eat the bowl.

00:05:00.198 --> 00:05:02.868
I hear a lot of families
are having family dance parties

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.437
to relieve stress and anxiety.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.906
It's fun until you're
dancing with your sister

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.273
and then Boyz II Men comes on.

00:05:08.273 --> 00:05:10.542
-♪ I'll make love to you ♪
-Alexa, next song!

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:13.612
-♪ Like you want me to ♪
-Alexa, next song!

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:16.449
And finally, a lot of people
are trying to buy new furniture

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:19.885
for working from home,
so if you and your spouse

00:05:19.885 --> 00:05:23.689
weren't fighting enough, try
assembling a new desk from IKEA.

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:26.992
That's our monologue, everybody!

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:28.995
♪♪

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:31.297
-Oh, hey, Jimmy.
-Hey, what's up, Jimmy?

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:33.198
How you doing?
-Everything's good.

00:05:33.198 --> 00:05:35.668
In quarantine, you know.
How about you?

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:38.871
-I'm just doing whatever
you're doing. You know?

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:41.974
-Well, I'm about to go get
my 14th snack of the day.

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:44.310
-I know. You want
to sing some harmony?

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:48.881
-Sure. One, two, three.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:54.854
-♪ It's like you're my mirror,
mirror staring back at me ♪

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:56.722
-A little pitchy.

00:05:56.722 --> 00:05:59.391
♪♪

00:05:59.391 --> 00:06:01.760
-Hey, guys, we're doing
this thing every Wednesday

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.195
where I show my favorite videos

00:06:03.195 --> 00:06:05.130
that people
have been putting online.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.933
It's called
"What Are You Doing Wednesdays."

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:09.935
♪♪

00:06:09.935 --> 00:06:11.804
We all know everyone's at home,

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:13.339
so here's what
you guys are doing.

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:15.007
This first guy
is celebrating his birthday.

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.776
This is how you celebrate
a birthday right now

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:19.278
in quarantine, 2020.
Take a look.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:24.183
-♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.885
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:28.788
-Blow out the candles!

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:30.856
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:34.493
-Well done. And a good audience,
by the way, too.

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:38.598
All those --
All those screens he has there.

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:41.033
These next two are grandparents.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.634
I think -- We think
they're grandparents.

00:06:42.634 --> 00:06:44.336
Either way, they're super cool.

00:06:44.336 --> 00:06:46.238
It's called
the Garage Door Challenge.

00:06:46.238 --> 00:06:49.475
They created a drinking game
using their garage door

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:54.079
to raise money and awareness
for directrelief.org.

00:06:54.079 --> 00:06:55.748
But check out these two.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.716
-Is it on?
-It's on.

00:06:57.716 --> 00:06:58.817
-All right! We're on!

00:06:58.817 --> 00:07:02.221
-Garage-door assisted corona...

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:04.389
-Chugging Challenge!

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:07.160
[ Whirring ]
-Get ready!

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:11.297
[Bleep]

00:07:17.202 --> 00:07:20.306
-Oh, [bleep].
[ Laughs ]

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:23.041
-I don't think we missed a drop.
-Jake and Barb...

00:07:23.041 --> 00:07:25.445
-I'm pretty sure we got it all.
-...you're up!

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:28.047
-Not my grandparents.
-Yeah, I know.

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:31.249
I love -- I love how they're,
like, shouting out,

00:07:31.249 --> 00:07:32.584
"All right, you're next."

00:07:32.584 --> 00:07:35.187
They're challenging other
people. They want to do it.

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:38.124
If I had an automatic garage
door, I would do it but I don't.

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:40.859
But anyways,
you're very fun people.

00:07:40.859 --> 00:07:45.197
This next video is --
Gosh. Do you love dogs?

00:07:45.197 --> 00:07:48.166
Do you love "Harry Potter"?
Well, here you go.

00:07:48.166 --> 00:07:51.303
This is bulldog "Harry Potter."

00:07:51.303 --> 00:07:57.009
♪♪

00:07:57.009 --> 00:08:02.714
♪♪

00:08:02.714 --> 00:08:06.352
-Wow. The CGI is so real.

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:09.921
The CGI was so real.
That was a flying dog.

00:08:09.921 --> 00:08:12.658
This last one is this couple --

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:14.827
I think they're a couple.
Could be brother and sister.

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.395
And she's just saying hey --

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:19.064
He's trying to practice
this golf trick indoors.

00:08:19.064 --> 00:08:22.101
And it's a trick
like Dude Perfect would do

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:24.636
or somebody,
but he pulls it off.

00:08:24.636 --> 00:08:26.272
Check it out.

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:29.108
-...swing and do it.
-Okay. Come on.

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:31.511
-God's sake.

00:08:33.078 --> 00:08:34.914
-Yeah! [ Laughs ]

00:08:34.914 --> 00:08:36.282
-Ohh!

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:40.253
Extra points for bouncing it off
of your girlfriend's head.

00:08:40.253 --> 00:08:44.557
Oh, my God. Guys, that was
"What Are You Doing Wednesday."

